<!--//

   if (document.images) {

      // Load images needed [BACK] button.

      back_on  = new Image(); back_on.src  = "../../buttons/back_on.gif";  
      back_off = new Image(); back_off.src = "../../buttons/back.gif";  
   }

   function TurnOn() {

      // Displays image and updates status bar.

      if (document.images) {
         document["back"].src = back_on.src;
         window.status = 'Go back to previous page';
      }
   }

   function TurnOff() {

      // Displays image and clears status bar.

      if (document.images) {
         document["back"].src = back_off.src;
         window.status = '';
      }
   }

//-->

</SCRIPT>

<H3><CENTER><FONT COLOR="#ffff00"><A HREF="mailto:richardellingham@hotmail.com">Richard Ellingham</A></FONT></CENTER></H3>

        Richard bought his Tipo 16V in January 2001. The car is a metallic red 3 door
	L reg, same as mine. The car probably has the lowest milage of any Tipo 16v
	in the UK - only 21,000. It's had a full Fiat service history all from the
	same garage where it was originally sold, and subsequently re-sold to
	Richard. The original asking price was &pound;4500 but Richard got it down
	to &pound;4000, which is still a fair amount, but considering the milage
	its ok.
	<P>
	The car won't need new dampers for a while, and its just had a brand new exhaust.
	However these parts will be removed soon, and replaced with similar items to
	those on <A HREF="ian_grist.html">Ian Grist's</A> car, so some good quality
	spares will be for sale. A new radiator has just been fitted.
	<P> 
        The down side is, the red stripes have faded, as have the badges. The drivers
	electric window motor is slower than manual windows. The oil pressure is too
	high. Richard has a few plans for the future money permitting. 

